 "title": "Discrete Mathematics and Its Applications (8th edition)",
 "byline": "Kenneth H. Rosen · McGraw-Hill Education, 2019",
 "note": "Summaries and terms are given per chapter; each section is listed with its PDF page range. End-of-chapter material, appendices and answers are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "The most widely used discrete mathematics textbook for computer science students. It covers logic and proof methods, sets, functions, sequences and matrices, algorithms and their complexity, number theory and cryptography, induction and recursion, counting, discrete probability, recurrences and generating functions, relations, graphs and trees, Boolean algebra and circuits, and models of computation from grammars and finite-state machines to Turing machines."
